3 Key Differences: Excel Dashboards vs Power BI Dashboards
| Feature                                 | Excel Dashboard                                                                                                 | Power BI Dashboard                                                                                                                                 |
| --------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **1. Data Modeling**                    | Usually relies on Excel tables, PivotTables, and formulas. Relationships between datasets are less centralized. | Has a dedicated **Model View** where multiple tables can be connected through relationships, making complex data models easier to manage.          |
| **2. Data Visualization & Interaction** | Uses charts, PivotCharts, slicers, and formulas. Interactivity is generally more limited.                       | Provides a wider range of interactive visuals, with cross-filtering, drill-down, slicers, and interactive report pages.                            |
| **3. Data Preparation & Refresh**       | Data cleaning is commonly done using formulas, PivotTables, or **Power Query**.                                 | **Power Query** is integrated directly into the workflow, and reports can be connected to multiple data sources and refreshed more systematically. |
